<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">@form Integration Pattern</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      When using the PDX <code>@form</code> rune, FormField reads validation state from the form object.
      The form handles all validation — FormField is purely presentational.
    </p>

    <div class="code-block">
      <pre class="pdx-txt-mono"><code>@form contact: {
  name: string { required, minLength: 3 },
  email: string { required, email },
}

&lt;pdx-form-field
  label="Name"
  required
  :error="contact.fields.name.error()"
  :touched="contact.fields.name.touched()"&gt;
  &lt;pdx-input
    :value="contact.fields.name.value()"
    @input="contact.fields.name.onChange($event.detail.value)"
    @blur="contact.fields.name.onBlur()"&gt;
  &lt;/pdx-input&gt;
&lt;/pdx-form-field&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</template>

<style scoped>
  .code-block { margin-top: var(--pdx-space-md); padding: var(--pdx-space-md); border: 1px solid var(--pdx-color-border); border-radius: var(--pdx-radius-md); background: var(--pdx-color-inset); overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-block pre { margin: 0; font-size: var(--pdx-text-xs); }
</style>
